theorem a-point-said-back-over-the-plane
  note        A letter bound over 𝔼² is a point. The kernel's set is ℂ
              for the plane and for the complex numbers alike, and a claim
              naming the letter where only a point may stand is said back
              over the plane, the domain under which it reads.
  let P be a point                                                    (H1)
  let Q be a point                                                    (H2)
  assume |PQ| = 1                                                     (H3)
  then there is H ∈ 𝔼² with |HQ| = 1

1.  there is H ∈ 𝔼² with |HQ| = 1
    exhibit, from H3
